  "question": "The electric field at a distance $r$ from an infinitely long straight wire with uniform linear charge density $\\lambda$ is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\lambda}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0 r^2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\lambda}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\lambda}{2\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\lambda}{2\\pi\\epsilon_0 r}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Gauss's law with a coaxial cylinder of length $L$: $E(2\\pi rL) = \\dfrac{\\lambda L}{\\epsilon_0} \\Rightarrow E = \\dfrac{\\lambda}{2\\pi\\epsilon_0 r}$.",
